    title: "What is HTML & How Browsers Read It",
    image: "public/HTML & CSS/Day_1.png",
    description:
      '🔥 Day 1: What is HTML? How Browser Reads It\n\nThe foundation of every website on the internet 🌐👇\n\n🔹 What is HTML?\n👉 Definition: HTML (HyperText Markup Language) is the standard language used to create and structure web pages.\n✔ Defines web page structure\n✔ Uses tags/elements\n✔ Tells browser what to display\n\n🔥 Simple HTML Example\n\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n <title>My Page</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n <h1>Hello HTML</h1>\n <p>Welcome to Web Development</p>\n</body>\n</html>\n\n🔹 Output in Browser\nHello HTML\nWelcome to Web Development\n\n🔹 What Does Browser Do?\nWhen browser receives HTML:\n1️⃣ Reads HTML file\n2️⃣ Parses tags\n3️⃣ Creates DOM Tree\n4️⃣ Applies CSS\n5️⃣ Executes JavaScript\n6️⃣ Renders webpage on screen\n\n🔥 How Browser Reads HTML?\nExample:\n<h1>Hello</h1>\n<p>World</p>\nBrowser creates:\nDocument\n └── html\n └── body\n ├── h1\n └── p\n\n👉 This structure is called:\n🌳 DOM (Document Object Model)\n\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n📘 HTML = Skeleton of a website\n🎨 CSS = Design & styling\n⚡ JavaScript = Functionality/behavior\n\n🔥 Browser Rendering Process\nHTML → DOM Tree\nCSS → CSSOM Tree\nDOM + CSSOM → Render Tree\nRender Tree → Screen Output\n\n🔹 Types of Browsers\n✔ Google Chrome\n✔ Firefox\n✔ Edge\n✔ Safari\n\nAll browsers have:\n✔ HTML Parser\n✔ CSS Engine\n✔ JavaScript Engine\n\n🔹 Why HTML is Important?\n✔ Foundation of web development\n✔ Required for frontend development\n✔ Used in every website\n\n👉 Browser downloads:\n✔ HTML\n✔ CSS\n✔ JavaScript\n✔ Images/videos\nThen builds webpage dynamically.\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nBrowser reads HTML from top to bottom line-by-line 🚀\n\n📌 Final Thought:\n"HTML gives structure to the web, and browsers transform it into visible webpages."',
