      '🔥 Day 3: Headings, Paragraphs & Formatting in HTML\n\nNow that we know the basic HTML structure, let\'s learn how to display content beautifully on a webpage 🌐✨\n\n🔹 What are Headings?\n👉 Headings are used to define titles and subtitles on a webpage.\nHTML provides 6 heading tags:\n<h1>Main Heading</h1>\n<h2>Sub Heading</h2>\n<h3>Section Heading</h3>\n<h4>Smaller Heading</h4>\n<h5>Minor Heading</h5>\n<h6>Smallest Heading</h6>\n\n🔥 Output\nMain Heading\n Sub Heading\n Section Heading\n Smaller Heading\n Minor Heading\n Smallest Heading\n\n👉 <h1> is the largest and most important heading.\n👉 <h6> is the smallest.\n\n🔹 What is a Paragraph?\n👉 The <p> tag is used to display text content.\nExample:\n<p>\n HTML is the foundation of web development.\n</p>\nOutput:\nHTML is the foundation of web development.\n\n🔥 Complete Example Program\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<head>\n <title>Formatting Example</title>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n <h1>HTML Basics</h1>\n <p>\n Welcome to HTML learning.\n </p>\n\n <p>\n <b>Bold Text</b><br>\n <i>Italic Text</i><br>\n <u>Underlined Text</u><br>\n <mark>Highlighted Text</mark><br>\n H<sub>2</sub>O<br>\n X<sup>2</sup>\n </p>\n\n</body>\n</html>\n\n🔥 Browser Output\n\nHTML Basics\nWelcome to HTML learning.\n\nBold Text\nItalic Text\nUnderlined Text\nHighlighted Text\nH₂O\nX²\n\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n📖 Headings = Chapter titles\n📄 Paragraphs = Content inside chapters\n🖍️ Formatting tags = Highlighters, bold markers, and styling tools\n\n🔹 Why Are They Important?\n✔ Improve readability\n✔ Better SEO\n✔ Proper content structure\n✔ Better user experience\n\n🔥 Interview Question\nQ: What is the difference between <b> and <strong>?\n✅ Answer:\n<b> makes text bold visually.\n<strong> makes text bold and indicates importance semantically.\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nUse only one <h1> per page for better SEO and page structure 🚀\n\n📌 Final Thought:\n"Headings organize content, paragraphs explain it, and formatting makes it engaging."',
