    image: "public/HTML & CSS/Day_4.png",
    description:
      '🔥 Day 4: Links & Navigation in HTML\n\nLinks are one of the most important features of the web 🌐\nImagine if websites had no links—you would have to manually type every URL to visit another page. Links connect web pages together and make browsing easy.\n\n🔹 What is a Link?\n👉 A link allows users to navigate between:\n✔ Web pages\n✔ Websites\n✔ Sections within a page\n✔ Files and documents\n✔ Email addresses\n\n🔹 What is Navigation?\n👉 Navigation is the process of moving between different pages or sections of a website.\nMost websites use navigation menus to help users find information quickly.\nExample:\n<nav>\n\n <a href="index.html">Home</a>\n\n <a href="about.html">About</a>\n\n <a href="services.html">Services</a>\n\n <a href="contact.html">Contact</a>\n\n</nav>\n\n🔥 Browser Output\nHome About Services Contact\n\n👉 Clicking any menu item takes the user to the corresponding page.\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n📖 Think of a website like a book.\n✔ Links = Page references\n✔ Navigation Menu = Table of Contents\nThey help readers quickly move to the information they need.\n\n\n🔹 Why Are Links Important?\n✔ Connect web pages together\n✔ Improve user experience\n✔ Help website navigation\n✔ Improve SEO structure\n✔ Make websites interactive\n\n🔥 Interview Question\nQ: Which HTML tag is used to create hyperlinks?\n✅ Answer:\nThe <a> (anchor) tag is used to create hyperlinks in HTML.\nExample:\n<a href="https://www.google.com">\n Visit Google\n</a>\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nAlways use meaningful link text like:\n✅ "Download Resume"\n✅ "Learn More About HTML"\nInstead of:\n❌ "Click Here"\nThis improves accessibility and SEO.\n\n📌 Final Thought:\n"Links connect the web, and navigation helps users explore it efficiently."',
