    description:
      '🔥 Day 5: Images & Media in HTML\n\nWeb pages become more engaging when they contain images, audio, and videos 🎨🎵🎬\n\nHTML provides simple tags to add multimedia content to your website.\n🔹 What are Images & Media?\n👉 Media refers to content such as:\n✔ Images 🖼️\n✔ Audio 🎵\n✔ Video 🎬\n✔ GIFs 🎭\n\nThese elements make websites more interactive and visually appealing.\n🔥 Adding Images in HTML\nImages are added using the <img> tag.\n<img src="nature.jpg"\n alt="Nature Image">\n\n🔹 Understanding Image Attributes\n<img src="nature.jpg"\n alt="Nature Image"\n width="300">\n\n🔥 Complete Image Example\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<body>\n <h1>My Favorite Place</h1>\n <img src="beach.jpg"\n alt="Beach Image"\n width="400">\n</body>\n</html>\n\n🔥 Browser Output\n\nMy Favorite Place\n[Beach Image Displayed]\n\n🔹 Why Use alt Attribute?\n<img src="nature.jpg"\n alt="Beautiful Nature">\nIf image cannot load:\nBeautiful Nature\nappears instead.\n✔ Improves accessibility\n✔ Better SEO\n✔ Helps screen readers\n\n🔥 Adding Audio\nHTML5 provides the <audio> tag.\n<audio controls>\n <source src="song.mp3"\n type="audio/mpeg">\n</audio>\n\n🔹 Browser Output\n▶️ Play | Pause | Volume\n\n🔥 Adding Video\nHTML5 provides the <video> tag.\n<video width="400"\n controls>\n <source src="movie.mp4"\n type="video/mp4">\n</video>\n\n🔹 Browser Output\n▶️ Play Video\nVideo player appears with controls.\n\n🔥 Complete Media Example\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<body>\n <h2>Image Example</h2>\n <img src="nature.jpg"\n alt="Nature"\n width="300">\n <h2>Audio Example</h2>\n <audio controls>\n <source src="song.mp3"\n type="audio/mpeg">\n </audio>\n <h2>Video Example</h2>\n <video width="400"\n controls>\n <source src="movie.mp4"\n type="video/mp4">\n </video>\n</body>\n</html>\n\n🔹 Supported Media Formats\nImages\n✔ JPG / JPEG\n✔ PNG\n✔ GIF\n✔ SVG\n✔ WebP\nAudio\n✔ MP3\n✔ WAV\n✔ OGG\nVideo\n✔ MP4\n✔ WebM\n✔ OGG\n\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n📰 Text = Newspaper article\n🖼️ Images = Photos in article\n🎬 Video = Live news report\n🎵 Audio = Radio broadcast\nTogether they improve the user experience.\n\n🔹 Best Practices\n✔ Use meaningful alt text\n✔ Optimize image size\n✔ Use responsive images\n✔ Avoid huge media files\n✔ Compress videos when possible\n\n🔥 Interview Question\nQ: Which HTML tag is used to display images?\n✅ Answer:\nThe <img> tag is used to display images.\nExample:\n<img src="image.jpg"\n alt="Sample Image">\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nAlways provide the alt attribute for accessibility and SEO benefits 🚀\n\n📌 Final Thought:\n"Images attract users, audio engages listeners, and videos create immersive web experiences."',
