      '🔥 Day 8: Forms Introduction in HTML\n\nForms are one of the most important features of a website 🌐\nWhenever you sign up, log in, search, or submit feedback, you\'re using an HTML form.\n\n🔹 What is a Form?\n👉 A form is used to collect user input and send it to a server for processing.\nExamples:\n✔ Login Form\n✔ Registration Form\n✔ Contact Form\n✔ Feedback Form\n✔ Search Form\n\n👉 Form sends data to server.\n\n🔹 Real-Life Analogy\n📝 Paper Application Form\nYou fill details → submit → organization processes information.\nHTML forms work exactly the same way.\n\n🔹 Why Forms Are Important?\n✔ Collect user data\n✔ User authentication\n✔ Online registrations\n✔ Search functionality\n✔ Feedback collection\n\n🔥 Interview Question\nQ: Which HTML tag is used to create a form?\n✅ Answer:\nThe <form> tag is used to create forms in HTML.\nExample:\n<form>\n <input type="text">\n</form>\n\n💡 Pro Tip:\nAlways use proper input types (email, password, number) because browsers provide built-in validation 🚀\n\n📌 Final Thought:\n"Forms are the bridge between users and web applications, enabling interaction and data collection."',
